From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Loading/Loaded/Unloaded, compiled x:Bind connections, XamlBindingHelper, Image

Elements never raised Loading, Loaded or Unloaded, so programs that do their work when a page is loaded did nothing (NanaZip refreshes its toolbar then). An element now raises Loading before it is first laid out in an island's tree (again for elements its layout makes, such as templates), Loaded after (children first) and Unloaded when it leaves; IsLoaded follows. Compiled templates are wired as compiled x:Bind expects: an element's x:ConnectionId reaches the component whose markup held the template (IComponentConnector); a ControlTemplate with an ID of its own is an x:Bind scope, and when it is applied the component's binding connector for it (IComponentConnector2.GetBindingConnector with the control) connects its elements too. XamlBindingHelper (new): the statics compiled x:Bind code calls -- SetPropertyFrom* (a boxed local value), ConvertValue (text as markup reads it), Get/SetDataTemplateComponent, Suspend/ResumeRendering. Framework type and property IDs newer than our table are dropped with one FIXME each instead of failing the file. Image (new) draws a SoftwareBitmapSource (SetBitmapAsync of a SoftwareBitmap: NanaZip's address bar icon) or a BitmapImage (UriSource or markup's Source="ms-appx:///...", decoded with WIC), Stretch None/Fill/Uniform/UniformToFill, centred. Our own interface probes no longer log FIXMEs. Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT); the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
